                        "review": "EPILEPSY FLASHING WARNING!\n\nNOT RECOMMENDED - maxing out every single location by grinding and spamming seeds is an extremely anti-fun process that needlessly pads out the game.\n\nIt has severe technical insufficiencies such as not being allowed to change the resolution without restarting and not centering the view on the player character to be worth playing. Changing the resolution is a standard feature. Having to restart means the developer did not bother to scale things properly on the fly. If you try to change the resolution or even switch to the windowed mode, the picture becomes messed up and possibly cropped. This is tutorial level stuff with Unity.\n\nMost of the objectives are poorly or not at all explained. For example, you are told to break the rocks with explosives, though you are never told what those explosives are. What you are actually supposed to do is to pick up red seeds and toss them around as makeshift explosives. This cripples the value of the narrative and downgrades it to a useless nuisance.\n\nThe whole plotline about some lost OCTO robot is extremely disappointing. It is one conversation that explains nothing. Also the ending cutscene is plain stupid and pointless.",
